WEBVTT

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.350
Quit being the Church's founder.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.400
You're not Silver Wolf, Nazuna.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.860
You don't need to act like
these lies are the truth.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.320
You see, Silver Wolf actually exists.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.320
So what?

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.570
I am the mistress of Silver Wolf,
Déesse Louve.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.370
Soon, there will be
more than 5,000 members

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.290
of my fan club, the Church.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.540
Some of my fans have sad lives,

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.670
but they say that just seeing me
gives them strength.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:33.420
Déesse Louve means hope
for people like that.

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:38.380
Besides, why did you come
to tell me about this anyway?

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:41.890
Did you want to criticize me
for being a fake?

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.850
No! I was just--

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:45.810
"I was just worried about you!"

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:48.560
There you go, forcing your beliefs
of what is just again.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:51.020
I'm already prepared for the consequences.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:56.820
Staying up late is bad for my skin,
so hurry up and leave.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.580
Shirou, how are your injuries?

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.630
You spoke to her, right?

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:15.760
Yes.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:19.090
Don't worry.
She doesn't know it's you, Shirou.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:30.600
You get depressed if you're hungry.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:34.480
People need to see and experience things
for themselves

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:36.780
before they find a satisfying answer.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:38.530
What?

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:42.030
I was just thinking that someone
who's lived 1,000 years sure knows a lot.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:43.950
Are you making fun of me?

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:45.950
Thank you.

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:47.950
I appreciate this.

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:04.470
I'm going to the police now
to find out more about Yaba.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.970
-Do you want to come?
-Not today.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:08.270
I have an errand to run.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.310
Stay away from the Church.

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:12.850
And Medi-Cen. Do you understand?

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:16.440
I understand. See you later!

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:51.730
The slum!

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.480
I thought it landed around here.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:03.450
Michiru!

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:04.950
What are you doing?

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:07.910
That's what I'd like to ask you.
What are those?

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:11.750
-Mineral water-esque water!
-What?

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:14.040
With the water purifier
I bought the other day...

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.130
You're still using that?

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:22.010
I will put this in and do this!

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:26.220
There! We have mineral water-esque water!

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.640
Water without garbage floating in it
is delicious!

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:35.650
-Do you want some, Michiru?
-No, but thanks anyway.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:37.810
I sell them for ten yen a bottle!

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:41.190
Wow! I'll become wealthy because of this!

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:49.580
There it is!

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.080
That's one of those Silver Wolf things!

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.330
I love the mistress of Silver Wolf!

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:57.830
I changed thanks to Silver Wolf.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:01.380
I no longer take flowers
from people's homes and sell them.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:05.840
And I don't take the saddles off bicycles
to sell anymore.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:08.470
You see, Silver Wolf is watching.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:10.810
Everyone living in the slum says so.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:14.770
Be the best beastman you can be.

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:16.270
But is doing that okay?

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:18.980
This is mineral water-esque water!

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:22.360
It's like the real thing!
It's not fake, and this is business!

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:25.530
I'm sick of hearing people say,
"Be the best beastman you can be."

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:28.410
Do you like Silver Wolf too, Michiru?

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:29.320
What?

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:34.830
Yes.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:36.370
I do like him.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.670
I found a ten-yen coin!

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:45.630
I have to show it to everyone!

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:48.680
She hasn't changed a bit.

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:59.150
Before Yaba changed like that,
he had been perfectly normal.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:18.580
That day, Yaba spent his morning as usual.

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:21.670
Then Boris from the Church
came to see him.

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:22.750
Boris?

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:26.050
He talked about giving the teachings
of God to criminals.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:30.340
The jail is destroyed,
and the vicious criminals have escaped.

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:33.720
I can't apologize enough for it.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.600
I want to see Yaba's corpse.

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:38.100
It was taken to the Medical Center.

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:41.350
To Medi-Cen? Isn't it the police's job
to do the forensics work?

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:46.320
It's also the police's job
to follow orders from higher up.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:00.830
Nazuna?

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:08.630
Nazuna!

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:33.450
Medi-Cen?

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:49.090
JAILED SUSPECT TRANSFORMS
INTO FRENZIED BEAST

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:55.640
-Are the results back from that test?
-Well, actually...

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:18.370
Nazuna!

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:23.080
Nazuna!

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:24.580
Michiru?

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:29.000
Are you all right?

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:34.340
What are you doing?

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:37.180
Only authorized personnel
are allowed here!

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:40.140
I've got all the authorization I need
to help Nazuna!

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:43.890
Don't, Michiru!

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:00.080
Take your hands off Nazuna!

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:03.750
You damn beast!

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:10.210
Michiru!

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.210
That's enough!

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:30.520
Michiru!

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:33.320
Release her.

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:40.620
What are you doing to Nazuna?

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:45.040
If anything happens to Nazuna,
there will be trouble with the Church!

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:47.710
In fact, I'll...

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:50.750
Your habit of jumping to conclusions
and causing trouble

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:53.170
hasn't changed a bit.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:01.100
I'm sorry. She must have thought
that I had been kidnapped.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:06.310
It's all right. That attitude
of acting recklessly to save a friend

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:08.140
is something I kind of like.

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:11.690
Nazuna, you've got
quite a good friend there.

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:13.610
You're Michiru, right?

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:16.070
I've heard a lot about you from Nazuna.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:18.860
I know you.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:20.620
<i>You're a Sylvasta bigwig.</i>

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:22.830
Well, what an honor.

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:26.290
That's exactly right. I am Alan Sylvasta.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:29.120
I'm the president
of Sylvasta Pharmaceutical.

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:31.960
What the heck is going on?

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:33.750
What are you doing here, Nazuna?

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:35.960
I was just getting an MRI.

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:37.760
"MRI"?

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:43.970
Nazuna is allowing us to study her
while we give her regular check-ups.

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:46.680
I came here of my own free will.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:48.680
Will you please leave?

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:51.850
Easy, now. Now that we have the chance,

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:55.230
maybe it's best
Michiru learned the truth as well.

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:56.610
But that's...

00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:59.780
If she draws conclusions from seeing
just part of the story,

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:01.530
it will cause trouble later.

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:04.490
And I think Michiru has the right to know

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:07.450
why she became a beastman.

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:10.960
Fine.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:12.920
Nazuna?

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:15.210
Michiru,

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:17.420
I need to apologize to you.

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:19.800
You became a beastman

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:22.930
because of this Medical Center.

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:30.640
You and Nazuna were accidentally given
a transfusion of an experimental drug

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:33.520
made from
activated beast deoxyribonucleic acid.

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:37.980
INFECTIOUS MEDICAL WASTE PRODUCTS

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:46.910
<i>Some of this experimental drug</i>
<i>accidentally got mixed in</i>

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:49.790
<i>with the drugs</i>
<i>that Yaba and Mimura sold illegally.</i>

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:52.080
GENERAL HOSPITAL

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:57.040
<i>It just happened</i>
<i>to get infused into you two.</i>

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.340
You must be kidding.

00:11:59.710 --> 00:12:02.840
When Yaba realized the number of bags
of medical waste didn't add up,

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:04.760
he desperately tracked it down.

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:08.140
He discovered that Nazuna
had transformed into a beastman,

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:10.350
so he rushed to capture
and quarantine her.

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:15.150
<i>But he didn't realize that you,</i>
<i>her friend, had transformed as well</i>

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:17.060
<i>until you arrived in this city.</i>

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:20.860
<i>The real reason they blew up Medi-Cen was</i>

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:24.030
<i>to destroy the data on the leak</i>
<i>of the experimental drug.</i>

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:27.530
<i>The development of the new drug</i>
<i>was top-secret.</i>

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:31.250
If anyone found out, they'd be punished
for more than illegally selling drugs.

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:33.460
If it hadn't been for you!

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:38.630
You mean Nazuna and I
are victims of your experiments?

00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:39.590
How awful!

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:40.920
I'm very sorry.

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:43.550
It is entirely my responsibility.

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:45.590
But don't worry.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:48.180
You can go back to being a human.

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:52.730
We're developing a drug
to cure the beastman disease.

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:54.560
It will be ready before long.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:58.230
With that, you and Nazuna can return
to being humans.

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:02.690
That's why I'm cooperating with Sylvasta.

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:16.620
<i>When I heard I'd been turned</i>
<i>into a beastman, I was shocked too.</i>

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:20.380
<i>But Sylvasta Pharmaceutical promised</i>
<i>that they would take</i>

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:24.420
<i>full responsibility and develop a drug</i>
<i>to turn me back into a human.</i>

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:28.090
<i>Until we're able to develop the drug</i>
<i>to heal the beastman disease,</i>

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:32.220
<i>I asked Nazuna to do the work</i>
<i>of giving hope to beastmen</i>

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.270
<i>by using her morphing abilities.</i>

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:40.360
Hold on!

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:44.190
You were against the Church
of the Silver Wolf coming to Anima-City!

00:13:44.570 --> 00:13:47.280
Oh, that. It was necessary to do so.

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:51.160
<i>To reduce the mental entropy</i>
<i>of the beastmen,</i>

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:53.870
<i>the Church of the Silver Wolf</i>
<i>is a necessity.</i>

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:56.710
What? "Entropy"?

00:13:57.080 --> 00:14:00.420
I'm sure you understand it,
now that you've lived in Anima-City.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.420
<i>Beastmen are easily influenced</i>
<i>by their emotions.</i>

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:05.210
<i>When their frustration builds up,</i>

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:08.720
<i>the slightest thing sends them</i>
<i>into a fury, causing confusion.</i>

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:13.310
We're using belief in Silver Wolf
to maintain their mental discipline.

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:18.440
Their mental entropy is reduced
by focusing solely upon God.

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:20.900
Isn't that the same as "stress"?

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:24.320
You see, since beastmen
have been oppressed by humans,

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:27.700
they'd never believe in a religion
that attracts humans.

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:31.870
<i>What about when you were saved</i>
<i>by Nazuna when you were attacked?</i>

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:35.870
<i>I knew ahead of time</i>
<i>that I might be attacked.</i>

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:38.830
<i>I simply used that information.</i>

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:42.750
A little acting is necessary
to get people to believe, you know.

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:46.170
The quickest way
to reduce their mental entropy

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:49.550
is to get the beastmen to choose
to believe on their own.

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:51.510
I think you mean "stress."

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:54.970
Mental entropy. Do you understand now?

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:00.230
You deceived everyone?

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:02.650
It was just an act.

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:06.190
As a result, order in Anima-City
has been maintained.

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:08.240
But why didn't you tell me?

00:15:08.650 --> 00:15:11.660
I told you I was looking for a way
to cure this beastman disease!

00:15:12.030 --> 00:15:14.370
It's top-secret, so of course, I couldn't.

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:17.040
Only Boris and I know about this.

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:19.290
You're an outsider,
so I couldn't tell you.

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:22.170
You and I are the ones
with beastman disease!

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:24.670
That creepy old guy is the outsider!

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:26.920
I told you, he's not that creepy!

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:30.670
Any old guy that sticks by you
around the clock is plenty creepy!

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:32.760
Easy, you two.

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:35.470
Everyone assumes
what they see is the truth.

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:37.390
It's the same with you.

00:15:37.810 --> 00:15:40.850
When you saw Nazuna getting
in a car with my people,

00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:43.230
you believed she had been kidnapped.

00:15:43.310 --> 00:15:45.440
But the truth was different, wasn't it?

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:49.900
The truth is where we can't see it.

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:54.200
I guarantee
that we'll make the drug for you.

00:15:55.070 --> 00:15:57.580
I swear that you'll return to being human.

00:15:58.160 --> 00:15:59.160
I promise.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:03.580
Can you please
cooperate with Nazuna until then?

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:13.300
"Cooperate"?

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:15.430
What am I supposed to do?

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:18.680
You should stop interfering with
what we're doing.

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:21.770
"We," you say?

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:54.030
I thought I told you to stay away
from the Church and Medi-Cen.

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:58.360
They said I'll be able to return
to being a human.

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:04.160
-A medical error?
-Yes.

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:07.660
But he apologized to me for it.

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:11.290
And he promised to make a drug for us.

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:13.460
You believe him?

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:16.510
He's just using you for his schemes.

00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:20.590
You only think that
because Alan is a human.

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:23.760
You doubt everything that humans say.

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:26.180
Your friend is human too, right?

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:29.390
She lies that she's Silver Wolf
and deceives beastmen.

00:18:29.480 --> 00:18:30.980
That's what humans are like.

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:33.940
You're wrong!
That's not what Nazuna is like!

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:37.740
I'll admit,
she's lying about being Silver Wolf.

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:41.910
Nazuna has always said
that she wanted to be a pop idol.

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:45.450
I thought she wanted
to be showered with attention.

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:48.460
Well, that's probably part of it.

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:53.420
<i>But Nazuna wants to give a glimmer</i>
<i>of hope and dreams to the beastmen</i>

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:56.380
<i>who've been persecuted</i>
<i>and suffered for so long.</i>

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:59.550
<i>That's why she became Silver Wolf</i>
<i>and works so hard.</i>

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:01.890
I think that's pretty amazing.

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:06.640
She wants me to overlook
that she's pretending to be Silver Wolf.

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:10.020
Did you join the Church?

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:14.360
Don't be ridiculous.
I don't believe in that bogus religion.

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:16.980
But I do believe in Nazuna.

00:19:17.730 --> 00:19:21.780
I realized that my feelings for her
haven't changed one bit.

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:26.580
It will tick her off,
so I'll never tell her that myself.

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:29.960
You want to go back to being a human?

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:31.210
What?

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:33.500
Yes, of course, I do.

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:36.880
If you do, will you leave Anima-City?

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:39.550
I've grown to love this city,

00:19:40.090 --> 00:19:42.840
but I want to go back home.

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:46.220
-Is that so?
-Yes.

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:52.850
Leave it open.

00:19:54.020 --> 00:19:57.150
The wind is cool tonight.
You'll catch a cold.

00:19:57.230 --> 00:19:58.110
I don't care.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:02.820
The tanuki girl won't be
coming here anymore, will she?

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:05.870
-Boris.
-Yes?

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:09.790
From now on, I'll have someone else
handle my affairs.

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:11.330
What? How come?

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:12.790
Because you're creepy!

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:17.500
And it's creepy that you enter my room
without permission,

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:19.130
so I prohibit it.

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:22.170
Be the best beastman you can be.

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:26.350
Be the best beastman you can be.

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:38.190
Ultimately, she's still human.

00:20:38.650 --> 00:20:40.530
-Did you say something?
-No.

00:20:40.610 --> 00:20:41.860
What brings you here today?

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:44.150
What's the forensics report on Yaba?

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:46.070
How did he end up that way?

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:48.620
His beast deoxyribonucleic acid
transformed.

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:52.700
-His beast deoxyribonucleic acid?
-We still don't know exactly why though.

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:55.540
When they do, they'll inform me.

00:20:55.620 --> 00:20:57.290
Why are you leaving this to Medi-Cen?

00:20:57.830 --> 00:21:01.630
I hate to admit it, but Medi-Cen
has the most advanced technology.

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:05.260
What's more, Alan isn't as bad as a human
as you think he is.

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:07.970
So everyone is friends with him now.

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:12.180
Since I was born,
I've never once met a good human.

00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:14.890
Really?
But you meet with one all the time.

00:21:15.350 --> 00:21:17.190
Isn't Michiru a good human?

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:26.570
Thank you very much for taking the time
out of your busy schedule.

00:21:27.110 --> 00:21:29.070
What is this urgent business of yours?

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:33.540
Without your assistance, Anima-City
never would have been established,

00:21:33.950 --> 00:21:35.540
Prime Minister Shiramizu.

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:38.250
That's why
I would like to consult with you.

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:39.500
Consult with me?

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:43.260
I have something I'd like to lend
to the Japanese government.

00:22:48.400 --> 00:22:50.490
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
